From: devteam builder <317464+saghul@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] client: h1: restart the guys queued on a connection that
 won't be kept alive

When an h1 response says the connection won't be kept alive (an HTTP/1.0
status line, or, with the Connection: close backport, a "Connection: close"
header), lws_client_interpret_server_handshake() takes every request queued
on that connection off its queue to restart them on connections of their
own.  On v5.0-stable that loop only moves them back to LRS_UNCONNECTED and
sets their user_space to NULL: nothing re-drives them, their timeout was
cleared when they were queued, and their user can no longer find them from
their callbacks.  The requests never go out and never settle.

Before the Connection: close backport this only bit HTTP/1.0 servers; with
it, any HTTP/1.1 server answering "Connection: close" while requests are
queued (eg, several fetches to one origin issued in the same tick) leaves
them hanging, where previously they failed fast with the leader.

Keep each dequeued guy's user_space and schedule him, through his
sul_connect_timeout (unused while he was queued), to restart from
lws_client_connect_2_dnsreq_MAY_CLOSE_WSI().  He goes solo there, since he
no longer pipelines, and if his connect fails he is closed and his user is
told.  Running from the event loop keeps the restart out of the leader's
handshake interpretation and the vhost lock it holds.

Not an upstream backport: this is specific to the v5.0-stable pin ac23cae70.
Upstream main replaces the transition with lws_wsi_event_role(ww,
LWS_WSIEV_RESTART, rops), which v5.0-stable does not have.  Drop this patch
on a bump once the target restarts the dequeued guys itself.
---
 lib/roles/http/client/client-http.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/roles/http/client/client-http.c b/lib/roles/http/client/client-http.c
--- a/lib/roles/http/client/client-http.c
+++ b/lib/roles/http/client/client-http.c
@@ -1048,6 +1048,22 @@ lws_http_is_redirected_to_get(struct lws *wsi)
 	return wsi->redirected_to_get;
 }
 
+/*
+ * A guy that was queued on a connection that turned out not to be kept alive
+ * has never had a connection of his own.  Restart him from connect2, where
+ * he will make one.  This runs from the event loop, not from inside the
+ * leader's handshake interpretation that dequeued him, and if the connect
+ * fails, he is closed and his user is told.
+ */
+static void
+lws_client_restart_dequeued(lws_sorted_usec_list_t *sul)
+{
+	struct lws *wsi = lws_container_of(sul, struct lws,
+					   sul_connect_timeout);
+
+	lws_client_connect_2_dnsreq_MAY_CLOSE_WSI(wsi);
+}
+
 int
 lws_client_interpret_server_handshake(struct lws *wsi)
 {
@@ -1492,7 +1508,13 @@ lws_client_interpret_server_handshake(struct lws *wsi)
 #endif
 #endif
 #endif
-				ww->user_space = NULL;
+				/*
+				 * Keep his user_space: it is his user's, and
+				 * the restart still reports to it
+				 */
+				lws_sul_schedule(ww->a.context, ww->tsi,
+						 &ww->sul_connect_timeout,
+						 lws_client_restart_dequeued, 1);
 			} lws_end_foreach_dll_safe(d, d1);
 			lws_vhost_unlock(wsi->a.vhost);
 		}
-- 
